Z||000000||DAVES85GT||10-12-2001||06:30 PM||||This may sound funny but I would actually like my fiero to be a bit quieter, I like the sound of the exhust but I do come home allot late at night and I know my neighbors hear me, well, Just bought my house and want the neighbors to be nice to me and not say "hey thats were the new guy lives with the noisey car!" I would rather people say " wow...thats a nice looking 85 GT fiero" It has megaphone tips on it right now, would it be quiter just buy replacing the tips?? I like the factory ones but would like it quiter....any input ???? thanks....<P><P>------------------<BR>DAVES<BR>85<BR>GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||10-12-2001||07:03 PM||||I'm not sure how to make it quieter. Never heard of anyone wanting to do that, actually. Make sure you don't have any holes in your exhaust. That would make it louder. If you're going to sell those tips, how much you want for them?<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">            <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||jelly2m8||10-12-2001||07:10 PM||||Get a aftermarket muffler from an exhaust shop, that will really quiet it down over the stock muffler||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rick 88||10-12-2001||09:36 PM||||You might try some resonated tips. They are available from ANSA, Matrix, Pacesetter, and others. Check out the Sport Compact ads and stores. These will quiet down your car. Some of the tips are very nice looking as well.<P>Rick 88||||reg||3
Z||000004||Pike||10-12-2001||09:42 PM||||You guys are so funny! You know that the tips are only for looks and have absolutely nothing to do with exhaust db...you kidders! I bet your just trying to see who you can suck in...aren't you?<P>Pike||||reg||1
Z||000005||DAVES85GT||10-12-2001||10:10 PM||||see I have herd mixxed stoires, I herd from some people that the "megaphone" tips amplify in some sorts the sound of the exhust? some say it just changes the sound? I am not one for a loud exhust but I have always have had and always will have a fiero, this is my second GT, but the exhust sound is no biggie just the loudness, I am more impressed by the fiero looks and the way it drives....  <P>------------------<BR>DAVES<BR>85<BR>GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||Philphine||10-12-2001||10:39 PM||||i just ground the megaphone part of my tips off a few days ago. i can't really tell any real sound difference. i want different tips and looking for 4 individual tips gives me more variety to choose from than looking for duals. sound wasn't really an issue but they didn't seem that loud to me anyway.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Rick 88||10-13-2001||12:05 AM||||Resonated tips can affect the exhaust note of a car compared to an open tip or pipe. The resonated tips contain an internal baffle packed with fiberglass like a "glass pack". This might be just enough attenuation to give you the sound level you are looking for.<P>Rick 88||||reg||1
Z||000008||btoth||10-13-2001||11:23 AM||||The tips do make a difference in the sound.  One of my friends had put cheap Walmart tips on his GT and it completely changed the sound.  No more burbling sound but more of a smooth sound.  I don't think it changed the deepness of the exhaust (is that the pitch?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) though.<P>Or you could always go to your local muffler place and just a one of those really quiet cheap mufflers.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 10-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||SLYGUY||10-13-2001||02:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rick 88:<BR><B>You might try some resonated tips. They are available from ANSA, Matrix, Pacesetter, and others. Check out the Sport Compact ads and stores. These will quiet down your car. Some of the tips are very nice looking as well.<P>Rick 88</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I put Ansa tips on my first car to make it louder and give it a unique sound. Granted, I was only eighteen at the time, but you could hear the car for at least a quarter mile. I would not recommend a "resonator" exhaust or tips as these seem to INCREASE the tone/volume of your exhaust.<P>Stick with the idea of an aftermarket muffler that will silence the tones that our factory resonator tips are amplifying.<BR>Good luck!<P>Sly||||reg||1
